00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
The camera pans across Fisherman's Horizon's unique architecture. Massive solar panel arrays cover much of the horizontal bridge platform.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Industrial cranes and lifting equipment rise at intervals. Metal railings and walkways connect the various structures. The entire town is built horizontally rather than vertically.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Small residential structures and buildings are integrated directly into the bridge framework. This is clearly a working-class community built for function, not luxury.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
The camera moves across walkways suspended over the ocean. Far below, water stretches to every horizon. Waves can be seen beneath the transparent or open sections of the platform.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The sun hangs low on the horizon, casting golden light across the ocean. The sky transitions from blue to orange and amber hues.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Squall and his team explore Fisherman's Horizon. They walk through the town, observing the peaceful industrial settlement and its inhabitants.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
A concert or musical performance scene develops. Squall and his friends stand on an improvised stage constructed from platform materials.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The band plays music for the assembled townspeople. The peaceful community watches the performance, offering a moment of respite and cultural exchange.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
The music and gathering symbolize the brief peace and connection between the travelers and the residents of Fisherman's Horizon.
